WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.233
HIPAA training. Module 3. The Privacy Rule: using and sharing patient information.

2
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.433
The Privacy Rule works like a locked door.

3
00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:14.933
Information may be used and shared only in the ways the rule lists.

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:22.067
Almost everything else needs the patient's written authorization, including marketing and sale.

5
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:27.033
Treatment, payment and healthcare operations are allowed without a form.

6
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:33.400
Sharing with the patient, and with HHS when it investigates, is always allowed.

7
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.633
Minimum necessary: send the invoice number and amount.

8
00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:43.200
Too much is sending the full chart to answer a billing question.

9
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.000
Before you send anything, ask five questions.

10
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.100
If any answer is not sure, do not send.

11
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.933
Who? Is the recipient the right, authorized person?

12
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.967
What? Is it only the minimum needed?

13
00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:02.633
Why? Is there a task-related reason?

14
00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:06.733
Where? Is it the approved system or address?

15
00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:10.667
How? Is the method approved and secure?

16
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:12.467
Stop.

17
00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:13.867
Do not share.

18
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:15.400
Ask your lead.

19
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.533
Now read the module.
